{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys includes three primitives for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createheldkeys","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHeldKeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an accessor that yields an array of all currently held key names."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys().length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys().join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In Solid, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHeldKeys()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an accessor function. Call it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"()"},{"type":"text","value":" to read the current value: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"heldKeys()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned array contains key names like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Shift'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Control'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Meta'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'A'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ArrowUp'"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createheldkeycodes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHeldKeyCodes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an accessor that yields a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values). Useful for distinguishing between left and right modifiers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <For each={Object.entries(heldCodes())}>\n        {([key, code]) => (\n          <div>\n            {key}: {code}\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"createkeyhold","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createKeyHold"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an accessor that indicates whether a specific key is currently held. Optimized to only trigger updates when the specified key's held state changes. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" argument can be a string or an accessor for reactive keys."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = createKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span classList={{ active: isShiftHeld() }}>Shift</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isCtrlHeld() }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isAltHeld() }}>Alt</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isMetaHeld() }}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hold-to-reveal UI"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem(props: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{props.file.name}</span>\n      <Show when={isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button class=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(props.file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n      <Show when={!isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(props.file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <Show when={isModHeld()}>\n      <div class=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n        <div>S - Save</div>\n        <div>Z - Undo</div>\n        <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n        <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n      </div>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"debugging-key-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging key display"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createHeldKeys,\n  createHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      <For each={heldKeys()}>\n        {(key) => (\n          <div>\n            <strong>\n              {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n            </strong>\n            <span class=\"code\">{heldCodes()[key]}</span>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <Show when={heldKeys().length === 0}>\n        <p>Press any key...</p>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"platform-quirks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform quirks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":" handles several platform-specific issues:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS modifier key behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyup"},{"type":"text","value":" event. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"window-blur","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Window blur"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three primitives subscribe to the singleton "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-store"},{"type":"text","value":". The tracker manages its own event listeners on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document"},{"type":"text","value":" and maintains state in a TanStack Store."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-held shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHotkeyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const visible = createHotkeyHint(() => binding()) // accessor: visible()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+Shift+[KeyK]"},{"type":"text","value":", holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ exact: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to require all binding modifiers, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ platform: 'mac' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"createheldkeys","text":"createHeldKeys","level":2},{"id":"createheldkeycodes","text":"createHeldKeyCodes","level":2},{"id":"createkeyhold","text":"createKeyHold","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","text":"Hold-to-reveal UI","level":3},{"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","text":"Keyboard shortcut hints","level":3},{"id":"debugging-key-display","text":"Debugging key display","level":3},{"id":"platform-quirks","text":"Platform quirks","level":2},{"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","text":"macOS modifier key behavior","level":3},{"id":"window-blur","text":"Window blur","level":3},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2},{"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","text":"Modifier-held shortcut hints","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys includes three primitives for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features.\n\n## `createHeldKeys`\n\nReturns an accessor that yields an array of all currently held key names.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys().length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys().join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> In Solid, `createHeldKeys()` returns an accessor function. Call it with `()` to read the current value: `heldKeys()`.\n\nThe returned array contains key names like `'Shift'`, `'Control'`, `'Meta'`, `'A'`, `'ArrowUp'`, etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed.\n\n## `createHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns an accessor that yields a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes (`event.code` values). Useful for distinguishing between left and right modifiers.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <For each={Object.entries(heldCodes())}>\n        {([key, code]) => (\n          <div>\n            {key}: {code}\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## `createKeyHold`\n\nReturns an accessor that indicates whether a specific key is currently held. Optimized to only trigger updates when the specified key's held state changes. The `key` argument can be a string or an accessor for reactive keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = createKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span classList={{ active: isShiftHeld() }}>Shift</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isCtrlHeld() }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isAltHeld() }}>Alt</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isMetaHeld() }}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem(props: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{props.file.name}</span>\n      <Show when={isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button class=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(props.file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n      <Show when={!isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(props.file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <Show when={isModHeld()}>\n      <div class=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n        <div>S - Save</div>\n        <div>Z - Undo</div>\n        <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n        <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n      </div>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createHeldKeys,\n  createHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      <For each={heldKeys()}>\n        {(key) => (\n          <div>\n            <strong>\n              {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n            </strong>\n            <span class=\"code\">{heldCodes()[key]}</span>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <Show when={heldKeys().length === 0}>\n        <p>Press any key...</p>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Platform quirks\n\nThe underlying `KeyStateTracker` handles several platform-specific issues:\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nOn macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the `keyup` event. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically.\n\n### Window blur\n\nWhen the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three primitives subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker` via `@tanstack/solid-store`. The tracker manages its own event listeners on `document` and maintains state in a TanStack Store.\n\n```tsx\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`createHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = createHotkeyHint(() => binding()) // accessor: visible()\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Key State Tracking Guide\nid: key-state-tracking\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys includes three primitives for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features.\n\n## `createHeldKeys`\n\nReturns an accessor that yields an array of all currently held key names.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys().length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys().join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> In Solid, `createHeldKeys()` returns an accessor function. Call it with `()` to read the current value: `heldKeys()`.\n\nThe returned array contains key names like `'Shift'`, `'Control'`, `'Meta'`, `'A'`, `'ArrowUp'`, etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed.\n\n## `createHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns an accessor that yields a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes (`event.code` values). Useful for distinguishing between left and right modifiers.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <For each={Object.entries(heldCodes())}>\n        {([key, code]) => (\n          <div>\n            {key}: {code}\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## `createKeyHold`\n\nReturns an accessor that indicates whether a specific key is currently held. Optimized to only trigger updates when the specified key's held state changes. The `key` argument can be a string or an accessor for reactive keys.\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = createKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span classList={{ active: isShiftHeld() }}>Shift</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isCtrlHeld() }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isAltHeld() }}>Alt</span>\n      <span classList={{ active: isMetaHeld() }}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem(props: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{props.file.name}</span>\n      <Show when={isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button class=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(props.file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n      <Show when={!isShiftHeld()}>\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(props.file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\n```tsx\nimport { createKeyHold } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = createKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <Show when={isModHeld()}>\n      <div class=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n        <div>S - Save</div>\n        <div>Z - Undo</div>\n        <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n        <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n      </div>\n    </Show>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createHeldKeys,\n  createHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = createHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      <For each={heldKeys()}>\n        {(key) => (\n          <div>\n            <strong>\n              {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n            </strong>\n            <span class=\"code\">{heldCodes()[key]}</span>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <Show when={heldKeys().length === 0}>\n        <p>Press any key...</p>\n      </Show>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Platform quirks\n\nThe underlying `KeyStateTracker` handles several platform-specific issues:\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nOn macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the `keyup` event. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically.\n\n### Window blur\n\nWhen the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three primitives subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker` via `@tanstack/solid-store`. The tracker manages its own event listeners on `document` and maintains state in a TanStack Store.\n\n```tsx\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/solid-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`createHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = createHotkeyHint(() => binding()) // accessor: visible()\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n"}
